---
args: { input: CaseInput }
returns: RunProposal
---
1. Bind `goal = await frameRequest(input)` from the request and `policy = await selectPolicy(input)` from supplied authority candidates. Preserve unresolved precedence instead of guessing which source governs.
2. Bind `work = await formTaskGraph(goal)` and `evidencePlan = await planEvidence(input, work)` so each operation has explicit prerequisites and a searched source universe.
3. Run the stages in their dependency order. The first stage receives only `input.domainRecords.firstStage`; every later stage receives the preceding function's actual accepted records. Bind each full result separately.
const recoverProcedureResult = await recoverProcedure(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan);
const mapLocalContextResult = await mapLocalContext(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, recoverProcedureResult.accepted);
const constructVariantResult = await constructVariant(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, mapLocalContextResult.accepted);
const replayProcedureResult = await replayProcedure(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, constructVariantResult.accepted);
const releaseInstructionResult = await releaseInstruction(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, replayProcedureResult.accepted);
4. Bind `stageSet: CaseStageSet = { recoverProcedure: recoverProcedureResult, mapLocalContext: mapLocalContextResult, constructVariant: constructVariantResult, replayProcedure: replayProcedureResult, releaseInstruction: releaseInstructionResult }` and `collection: CollectionFinding = await reconcileCollection(stageSet)`. Bind `allQuestions: string[] = [...recoverProcedureResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...mapLocalContextResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...constructVariantResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...replayProcedureResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...releaseInstructionResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...collection.coverageGaps]` and `questions: QuestionBatch = await resolveQuestions(allQuestions, input)`.
5. Bind `invalidation = await assessDelta(input)`, `review = await prepareReview(collection)`, and `view = await composeView(review, input)`; pass each child its actual declared inputs and retain the returned object.
6. Bind `allChecks: CheckResult[] = [...recoverProcedureResult.checks, ...mapLocalContextResult.checks, ...constructVariantResult.checks, ...replayProcedureResult.checks, ...releaseInstructionResult.checks]`. Bind `hasGateFailure = allChecks.some(check => check.verdict !== "pass")` and `hasBlocker = input.authorityStatus !== "authorized" || questions.questions.length > 0 || collection.coverageGaps.length > 0`. Bind `disposition: "proposed" | "blocked" | "needs-review" = hasBlocker ? "blocked" : hasGateFailure ? "needs-review" : "proposed"`. Bind `rationale: string[] = allChecks.map(check => `${check.check}: ${check.verdict}; evidence ${check.evidenceIds.join(",")}`)`.
7. Operational detail 1 — A printed instruction remains on the floor: include version identifiers and a withdrawal task. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (include version identifiers and a withdrawal task.) through the existing stage result for ProcedureRequirement; preserve exact source/version and the prior ProcedureRequirement, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
8. Operational detail 2 — A local term names two controls: require unambiguous equipment references. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (require unambiguous equipment references.) through the existing stage result for ProcedureRequirement; preserve exact source/version and the prior ProcedureRequirement, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
9. Operational detail 3 — A translation shortens a warning: verify semantic preservation before release. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (verify semantic preservation before release.) through the existing stage result for ProcedureRequirement; preserve exact source/version and the prior ProcedureRequirement, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
10. Operational detail 4 — A procedure is interrupted mid-step: specify restart and re-verification conditions. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (specify restart and re-verification conditions.) through the existing stage result for ProcedureRequirement; preserve exact source/version and the prior ProcedureRequirement, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
11. Operational detail 5 — A local exception waives a queue but not an inspection: preserve the inspection guard explicitly. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (preserve the inspection guard explicitly.) through the existing stage result for ProcedureRequirement; preserve exact source/version and the prior ProcedureRequirement, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
12. Initialize `revisions: RevisionProposal[] = []`. If any gate is not pass, bind `revision = await proposeRevision(the failed check names, the smallest affected stage name)` and add that returned proposal to revisions. Bind and return `result: RunProposal = { caseId: input.caseId, goal, policy, work, evidencePlan, recoverProcedure: recoverProcedureResult, mapLocalContext: mapLocalContextResult, constructVariant: constructVariantResult, replayProcedure: replayProcedureResult, releaseInstruction: releaseInstructionResult, collection, questions, invalidation, review, view, revisions, disposition, rationale }`. Proposed actions remain proposals. The host owns authorization, persistence, effect dispatch and verification.
